#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spherical_harmonic_y

#% text
# `spherical_harmonic_y(l, m, theta, phi)` gives the spherical harmonic Y_l^m(theta, phi).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For integers l >= 0 and |m| <= l, in terms of cos(theta), sin(theta) and exp(i m phi); zero for |m| > l.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spherical_harmonic_y(1, 0, t, p)
#% output
#= cos(t)*3^(1/2)/(2*pi^(1/2))

#% cell
spherical_harmonic_y(1, 1, t, p)
#% output
#= -6^(1/2)*exp(im*p)*sin(t)/(4*pi^(1/2))

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
spherical_harmonic_y(2, -1, 0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.3105211711209513 - 0.09605545449894311im

